From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:08:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smp2p_sleepstate: wakeup events only while
 suspending

The DSPs toggle the inbound sleepstate entry many times a second while
sensors stream. Each edge reported a 200 ms wakeup event, so the wakeup
source stayed active for as long as a sensor client was open, and a
read of /sys/power/wakeup_count blocks while any wakeup source is
active. KDE's powerdevil reads it through a helper before every
suspend: the helper hung until the 25 s D-Bus timeout, so a closed
cover put the tablet to sleep only after ~26 s (and not at all if the
cover was opened again within that time).

The wakeup event only matters once a suspend has started: from
PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE (this notifier runs first) to PM_POST_SUSPEND it
aborts the suspend or wakes the system as before. Outside that window
the edges are ignored.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p_sleepstate.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p_sleepstate.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p_sleepstate.c
index 70f1a4e6e..139a465a4 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p_sleepstate.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p_sleepstate.c
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ struct smp2p_sleepstate {
 	struct qcom_smem_state *state;
 	struct wakeup_source *ws;
 	struct notifier_block pm_nb;
+	bool suspending;
 };
 
 static int smp2p_sleepstate_pm_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb,
@@ -33,10 +34,12 @@ static int smp2p_sleepstate_pm_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb,
 
 	switch (event) {
 	case PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE:
+		WRITE_ONCE(ss->suspending, true);
 		qcom_smem_state_update_bits(ss->state, AWAKE_BIT, 0);
 		break;
 	case PM_POST_SUSPEND:
 		qcom_smem_state_update_bits(ss->state, AWAKE_BIT, AWAKE_BIT);
+		WRITE_ONCE(ss->suspending, false);
 		break;
 	}
 
@@ -47,7 +50,16 @@ static irqreturn_t smp2p_sleepstate_handler(int irq, void *data)
 {
 	struct smp2p_sleepstate *ss = data;
 
-	__pm_wakeup_event(ss->ws, 200);
+	/*
+	 * Only a suspend in progress needs to hear that the DSP wants the AP
+	 * awake. While the system is running, the DSP toggles this entry
+	 * many times a second when sensors stream; a wakeup event for each
+	 * edge kept the source active all the time, and a read of
+	 * /sys/power/wakeup_count blocks while any source is active (KDE's
+	 * powerdevil waited 25 s before every suspend).
+	 */
+	if (READ_ONCE(ss->suspending))
+		__pm_wakeup_event(ss->ws, 200);
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
